[{:db/id "q-275781/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "2cf19437-06f3-5ea2-9f83-78e1cabbc712" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284860 :answer-field/choices ["q-275781/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78551/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "125c1985-9152-5da8-abc1-0fa65030f129" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78551/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "78413cf9-4770-5672-a06b-5c736541e297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78551/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "cea4aaeb-7ba5-5cc5-b409-5efa13136c72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78551/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "9535c375-2d54-5e41-a8f0-e3d677a695ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78551/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "442dac3f-64fb-54c6-b5d4-53c435ee3c63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78551/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6036be45-3f7b-5236-9670-640a998a7124" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78551/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-78551/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-78551/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-78551/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-78551/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-78551/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78551" :question/id #uuid "6b5a6d2e-84ca-5b1b-8229-e89b616a1853" :question/math-academy-id "q-78551" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ 3x+2y-z=1 \\\\ x-4y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -14 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -14 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=-2,z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+(-2)+(-2)=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78551/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78551"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78554/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "9aa84d7d-1757-5dea-8820-f54c350e31d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78554/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "fe2acb76-b360-5d36-8279-07de89647b6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78554/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b8fabc54-cb32-5fe2-8133-9a3dade1fbe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78554/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "7552d8e9-5a32-5505-aa29-6312c454d7d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78554/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "17c06854-3e2a-5643-9ab9-adfc84f159f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78554/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "473d2ff0-b888-5fba-b140-c20e73e280c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78554/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-78554/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" "q-78554/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-78554/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-78554/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-78554/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78554" :question/id #uuid "b1c000e5-dd9a-5906-a229-6843cfbdf8cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-78554" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z=0 \\\\ x+3y+z=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y-z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $\\frac{yz}{x}?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=-1,y=-1,z=3.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{yz}{x}=\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 3}{-1}=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78554/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78554"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78421/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "29842345-b6c2-5d6d-9d82-89a73f9b97e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78421/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "356ed408-1e33-568a-bd26-e3307d2b9b8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78421/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "864583e4-523f-5dfa-880c-aec63263656e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78421/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c74ce52f-ebd5-5b5a-8ff2-96579f6a2943" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78421/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "73afc0ce-73e9-5fc7-8fbe-f9ac34f81ae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78421/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d49f56c9-7e65-583a-b934-0a287de9762e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78421/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-78421/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-78421/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-78421/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-78421/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-78421/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78421" :question/id #uuid "db6060ad-8c77-548e-9bad-ddb7a1172d78" :question/math-academy-id "q-78421" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z=1 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=-1,z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+(-1)+(-2)=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78421/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78421"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10076/selection/ae8b724cd4f61221423bc942c2e3dc9fab74f088ae4864a20d45e71c443db3f8" :answer/id #uuid "ee0c1bfc-c0b0-5476-9eff-a10057ad340a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=15,y=-49,z=-58" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10076/selection/99544ce248f299558df3b04f1ce958c3d2d4b75148cf80d0c8fdf374cb35e9b3" :answer/id #uuid "d84f689a-134f-5407-b5f7-e046f6e72b21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10076/selection/b46ccc28444d71eea61b4a35e097a8556efc11d4f9d407eab181d92dc0603b94" :answer/id #uuid "49684f5f-864b-59c5-b876-5b3a8697f322" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=19,y=49,z=58" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10076/selection/019fa764d1e0838e47201f32de2189df00ebc674820680bea86c17e7e3f60853" :answer/id #uuid "455280a6-f859-5054-803b-696ef3129529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=42,y=-35,z=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10076/selection/e1fd412a2c8f936e49d4afa0937824b36027b8d4c7a827e7432898733b89258a" :answer/id #uuid "ac85153a-3e2f-5e94-8d8d-4602905ebb9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10076/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1033273-5d4f-5a9d-b005-946c4dd7384e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10076/selection/e1fd412a2c8f936e49d4afa0937824b36027b8d4c7a827e7432898733b89258a" :answer-field/choices ["q-10076/selection/ae8b724cd4f61221423bc942c2e3dc9fab74f088ae4864a20d45e71c443db3f8" "q-10076/selection/99544ce248f299558df3b04f1ce958c3d2d4b75148cf80d0c8fdf374cb35e9b3" "q-10076/selection/b46ccc28444d71eea61b4a35e097a8556efc11d4f9d407eab181d92dc0603b94" "q-10076/selection/019fa764d1e0838e47201f32de2189df00ebc674820680bea86c17e7e3f60853" "q-10076/selection/e1fd412a2c8f936e49d4afa0937824b36027b8d4c7a827e7432898733b89258a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10076" :question/id #uuid "1f56f052-82ef-5f6f-b9cb-411952681c67" :question/math-academy-id "q-10076" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z=9 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ -49 \\\\ -58\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=19,y=-49,z=-58.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10076/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78566/selection/bae2a82734d751af89897db18b0455820aece6c2275be3d10ee697c5e7869a83" :answer/id #uuid "cc8d39a5-78b9-5d1e-95d5-fe61d3ed1f5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78566/selection/228383024b3593d05de37eed2bb562e0d6a730857df66d9c3955eedff4ae2960" :answer/id #uuid "7f791699-f330-5e27-be89-31bb2628e35e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=BA\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78566/selection/c822a3635f9151eae99cc4f85624072a4ea0b574600ddb4dd37b274d1a11435c" :answer/id #uuid "366f4140-c8bb-5bb1-afee-426a78f9bc2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78566/selection/2368b2e13ee88e206eb3943d41cca061e39ac84490a23cca5931de1ebda2cb42" :answer/id #uuid "24c2ebf6-4fc7-546c-bf5f-a9da60c5f3ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=d\\,AB" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78566/selection/0d61b819d3b8b7f6bc9f5eeae7a111cba6f55e8815d68dff3572972d2513f95e" :answer/id #uuid "f91a107e-9f80-5278-a498-ecf78c338881" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=AB\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78566/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3757bf-b37c-5fcf-a6c9-45c2b4ba907e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78566/selection/228383024b3593d05de37eed2bb562e0d6a730857df66d9c3955eedff4ae2960" :answer-field/choices ["q-78566/selection/bae2a82734d751af89897db18b0455820aece6c2275be3d10ee697c5e7869a83" "q-78566/selection/228383024b3593d05de37eed2bb562e0d6a730857df66d9c3955eedff4ae2960" "q-78566/selection/c822a3635f9151eae99cc4f85624072a4ea0b574600ddb4dd37b274d1a11435c" "q-78566/selection/2368b2e13ee88e206eb3943d41cca061e39ac84490a23cca5931de1ebda2cb42" "q-78566/selection/0d61b819d3b8b7f6bc9f5eeae7a111cba6f55e8815d68dff3572972d2513f95e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78566" :question/id #uuid "e9038fac-5f35-5ebb-bf51-e55eda35beaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-78566" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x=d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $3\\times 3$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x=d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{3}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${B}^{-1}\\,x=A\\,d$ by $B,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1}\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ B{B}^{-1}\\,x & =BA\\,d \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,x & =BA\\,d \\\\ x & =BA\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78566/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78563/selection/77fea2f83372ed9f90b5ab2690b6f425d5598a0f74cb378e2d37776685853511" :answer/id #uuid "5790b096-f0ce-5afc-bfb8-66f8573cd6d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=d\\,{A}^{-1}B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78563/selection/63875f462eaa5a4f7c7dd738a0fe159658214a3db787653ac9c6f2b17eb1d8c0" :answer/id #uuid "eb7f731e-bcdb-5099-ba3c-b6da5b2d0b6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}B\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78563/selection/b1d03968802a438a45e3feff90688a1d2be61935102210fac0de5ae74c6e61e6" :answer/id #uuid "10777031-1f86-5194-b6f8-92deeb7e7339" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=B\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78563/selection/eee46017f28706d8a739ee8d33b21621a284ac089bd08b305342f5c29667abf3" :answer/id #uuid "93c4d244-6e10-5249-b01a-27a323f6d7af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}\\,d\\,B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78563/selection/e472aecf20d2cd5f0e251ef5d584b24ad0b47241a56a31d04ed07656c00b18c1" :answer/id #uuid "3496926d-e3dc-5f49-95f0-f444cd83a071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=B{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78563/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d53b8af-4f7a-5df4-bee8-6dfc934aacc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78563/selection/63875f462eaa5a4f7c7dd738a0fe159658214a3db787653ac9c6f2b17eb1d8c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-78563/selection/77fea2f83372ed9f90b5ab2690b6f425d5598a0f74cb378e2d37776685853511" "q-78563/selection/63875f462eaa5a4f7c7dd738a0fe159658214a3db787653ac9c6f2b17eb1d8c0" "q-78563/selection/b1d03968802a438a45e3feff90688a1d2be61935102210fac0de5ae74c6e61e6" "q-78563/selection/eee46017f28706d8a739ee8d33b21621a284ac089bd08b305342f5c29667abf3" "q-78563/selection/e472aecf20d2cd5f0e251ef5d584b24ad0b47241a56a31d04ed07656c00b18c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78563" :question/id #uuid "f46dcea5-1f8c-5ca6-bcf8-024327ec2e37" :question/math-academy-id "q-78563" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $A\\,x=B\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A\\,x=B\\,d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\,x & =B\\,d \\\\ {A}^{-1}A\\,x & ={A}^{-1}B\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}B\\,d \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}B\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78563/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78563"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4520"] :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/add80202102548e61880979bc0379e0bc65f9ef7fa37173f9035410661e2b75e.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4521"] :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/97d3c148b792d9db50bc81b8c12f1574f284746cb37b12d99a8881853bf5ea13.png)\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/e93ae11a2b2d1538c4ad97bba6d92e8e17fe14c8778898365ffeda9c5d1bacee.png)\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/c2492650916d7a880ea52322edb41b8127b4c31bcff0620cec3cf4e37fa7928f.png)\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/dd70742ae3c6613f78305edc718b10568269b49be611643059a1e6121828f404.png)\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
